From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [RFC PATCH 2/2] firmware: arm_scmi: set up Tx/Rx channel for
 ACPI-activated protocols

Patch 1/2 activates every firmware-implemented SCMI protocol under ACPI,
because the ACPI namespace has no per-protocol child nodes to drive
scmi_create_protocol_devices() from the DT path.

However it creates each protocol's device WITHOUT first setting up that
protocol's Tx/Rx channel. On DT this is done by scmi_txrx_setup() before
scmi_create_protocol_devices(). Without the channel setup the protocol
has no entry in info->tx_idr, so do_xfer() -- which outside RAW mode has
no Base-channel fallback -- returns -EINVAL for every transfer on that
protocol. The protocol is silently non-functional even though its device
was created.

The most damaging instance is SCMI_PROTOCOL_POWER (0x11): it registers no
power domains, so genpd consumers touch unpowered MMIO and hang (a
multi-second AXI lock was observed on an arm64 test platform before the
watchdog recovered). Protocols that do not depend on genpd are silently
degraded rather than fatal.

Mirror the DT path: call scmi_txrx_setup(info, NULL, prot_id) for each
ACPI-activated protocol before creating its device. Under ACPI there is
no per-protocol channel fwnode, so pass NULL; mailbox_chan_available(NULL,
idx) returns false and scmi_chan_setup() takes the Base-channel alias
path (no fwnode dereference), which matches how a single shared transport
serves all protocols on these platforms.

Not-yet-Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/driver.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/driver.c b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/driver.c
index b38d76461f39..1b99613xxxxxx 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/driver.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/driver.c
@@ -3383,6 +3383,17 @@ static int scmi_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			if (idr_find(&info->active_protocols, prot_id))
 				continue;

+			/* Set up the protocol's Tx/Rx channel before creating its
+			 * device.  Under ACPI there's no per-protocol channel node;
+			 * pass NULL fwnode so scmi_chan_setup() aliases this protocol
+			 * to the Base channel.  do_xfer() has no Base fallback outside
+			 * RAW mode, so without this the protocol has no tx_idr entry
+			 * and every xfer returns -EINVAL, silently killing genpd
+			 * (SCMI_PROTOCOL_POWER 0x11) -> consumer MMIO hang.
+			 */
+			if (scmi_txrx_setup(info, NULL, prot_id))
+				continue;
+
 			ret = idr_alloc(&info->active_protocols, (void *)np,
 					prot_id, prot_id + 1, GFP_KERNEL);
 			if (ret != prot_id)
